### WebSocket chat via one-time ticket (browser-usable auth).
### Run http/auth.http first so {{oauthToken}} is set.
### Syntax per JetBrains docs "WebSocket requests": https://www.jetbrains.com/help/idea/http-client-in-product-code-editor.html#websocket
### - the body of a WEBSOCKET request is the first frame sent on connect
### - `=== wait-for-server` before the next message = wait for one server frame first
### - received frames are shown in the Services tool window (no scripted assertions on WS frames)

### 1) Mint a single-use ticket (256-bit, 10 s TTL, redeemable exactly once)
POST {{host}}/ws-ticket
Authorization: Bearer {{oauthToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("wsTicket", response.body.ticket)
    client.log("ws ticket minted, expires in " + response.body.expiresIn + "s")
 %}

### 2) Connect and chat: sends the first frame on connect, waits for one server
### frame (HANDSHAKE), sends a second frame, waits for the next (your user id),
### then sends a broadcast. ALL echo comes back — `from` is server-stamped with
### your user id, not the value you sent. Answer pings with the pong frame.
WEBSOCKET ws://localhost:8080/ws?ticket={{wsTicket}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"to":"ALL","content":"hello from IntelliJ HTTP Client"}

=== wait-for-server
{"to":"ALL","content":"second frame after one server frame"}

=== wait-for-server
{"to":"ALL","content":"broadcast after second server frame"}

=== wait-for-server
=== wait-for-server
{"to":"SYSTEM","content":"pong"}

### 3) Negative: ticket replay -> upgrade rejected with 401 BEFORE the handshake
### (run immediately after request 2 consumed the ticket)
WEBSOCKET ws://localhost:8080/ws?ticket={{wsTicket}}

{"to":"ALL","content":"replay - expect 401 error"}

### 4) Negative: foreign Origin -> 403 before the handshake.
### Mint a fresh ticket first (a foreign-Origin attempt does NOT consume it),
### then this request shows the 403; the same ticket still works afterwards (5).
POST {{host}}/ws-ticket
Authorization: Bearer {{oauthToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("wsTicketOrigin", response.body.ticket)
 %}

###
WEBSOCKET ws://localhost:8080/ws?ticket={{wsTicketOrigin}}
Origin: http://evil.example

{"to":"ALL","content":"expect 403 Forbidden"}

### 5) The ticket survived the 403: allowed Origin (or none) connects fine
WEBSOCKET ws://localhost:8080/ws?ticket={{wsTicketOrigin}}

{"to":"ALL","content":"expect 101 + HANDSHAKE frame"}
